 "researcher_notes": "East Tennessee Jewell Ridge Lateral is not an existing row. The main line is P0179 and the other East Tennessee rows are different expansion projects. The 2026 August EIA release (Historical Projects sheet, Excel row 409) lists a completed 2006 lateral in Virginia: 32 miles of new 20-inch pipe, 235 MMcf/d, FERC docket CP05-413. A December 2005 Federal Register notice and an Oil and Gas Journal article agree on the 32-mile 20-inch lateral from the East Tennessee system to the Cardinal States gathering system in Tazewell County, Virginia, with 235 MMcf/d. The Oil and Gas Journal article reports it placed in service. FERC granted the certificate in February 2006. Length is about 51.5 km, above the 25 km rule. EIA is one origin, so the FERC notice and the trade press are the independent pairing. Parent system name follows the P0179 spelling. Owner spelled as the sources spell it; no legal form found. Exact start point and the end point name were not confirmed. No route was found, so the route is marked unavailable. Confidence high."
